.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-analytics-summary - Headline figures: orders, disputes, refund/dispute rates, volume


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 analytics summary [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Headline figures for the account: order count, disputed count, refund and
dispute rates, per-status counts, and volume.

.PP
Volume here is broken out per (token, chain), so it never hits the problem its
siblings warn about: each figure has a single unit behind it and is safe to read
directly. 'timeseries' and 'breakdown' return null volumes instead wherever a
row would span more than one token, since summing different tokens' base units
would produce a number that looks addable and is not.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chain\fP=
	Filter by chain: a slug (arc, base, …) or a chain id; the environment's gateway decides testnet vs mainnet

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	Only payments created at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for summary

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Filter by mode: authorize or charge

.PP
\fB--payee\fP=""
	Restrict to one of your account's wallets (0x address or @alias); default: the whole account

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Filter by payment status (e.g. captured)

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	Only payments created at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	Filter by token address (0x…)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 analytics summary --chain arc
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-analytics(1)\fP
